    <string name="about_version">Version %1$s</string>
    <string name="about_tagline">A launcher for Fire TV, by simplemal.</string>
    <string name="about_independent">Independent project</string>
    <string name="about_independent_text">Salotto is not affiliated with, sponsored by or endorsed by Apple, Amazon or the other brands mentioned.</string>
    <string name="about_goals">Goals and features</string>
    <string name="about_clean">Cleaner.</string>
    <string name="about_clean_text">The Fire TV Home puts ads, recommended content and autoplay videos in front of your apps. Salotto shows only your apps, the backdrop, the time and the weather. No ads and no offers.</string>
    <string name="about_private">Less tracking.</string>
    <string name="about_private_text">Installing turns off the advertising, telemetry and Alexa packages, limits the advertising ID and stops usage data from being sent. If a Fire OS update turns them back on, Salotto tells you and you can turn them off again. Salotto connects only to Open-Meteo for the weather and to GitHub for updates.</string>
    <string name="about_others">With programs from others.</string>
    <string name="about_others_text">FireStick Fixer brings the Home key to Salotto. AirPlay Server receives from iPhone, iPad and Mac. Aurora Store installs Android apps, even without an account.</string>
    <string name="about_only">Only in Salotto.</string>
    <string name="about_only_text">Illustrated or photographic backdrops that follow your city’s weather and time. A control center over any app, by holding down Home: Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, timer, brightness and blue light filter. A task manager by holding down Back. A page with the audio and video standards of the Stick and the TV. Clearer dialogue and even volume at your fingertips: they are Fire OS filters, gathered in one place. Signed updates, checked before they are installed.</string>
    <string name="about_license">License</string>
    <string name="about_license_text">PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0. Salotto can be used, studied, modified and built upon for free for non-commercial purposes. To sell it you need the author’s permission.</string>
    <string name="about_marks">Trademarks</string>
    <string name="about_marks_text">All trademarks belong to their respective owners. Fire TV, Alexa, Prime Video and Amazon are trademarks of Amazon. Android and Google Play are trademarks of Google. AirPlay, AirPods, HomePod and Apple TV are trademarks of Apple. Netflix, Dolby, Dolby Vision, Dolby Atmos, HDMI, Bluetooth, Wi-Fi and the other names mentioned belong to their owners. This project is not affiliated with any of them, nor endorsed by them.</string>
